            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter embolization of an internal mammary artery bypass graft sidebranch causing coronary steal syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 66-yr-old man with angina after internal mammary artery-coronary bypass grafting due to coronary artery steal by a sidebranch of the mammary artery. Myocardial ischemia was successfully treated by transcatheter embolization of the sidebranch.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
